§ `The combinator: an exclusion first, then an inclusion, otherwise NOTHING`

#ASSERT `Art 2 the Regulation applies given the answers of the paragraphs` (LIST (JUST TRUE), NOTHING) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 2 the Regulation applies given the answers of the paragraphs` (LIST NOTHING, (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 2 the Regulation applies given the answers of the paragraphs` (LIST (JUST TRUE), (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 2 the Regulation applies given the answers of the paragraphs` (LIST (JUST FALSE), (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 2 the Regulation applies given the answers of the paragraphs` (LIST (JUST FALSE), NOTHING) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 2 the Regulation applies given the answers of the paragraphs` (LIST NOTHING, NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 2 the Regulation applies given the answers of the paragraphs` (EMPTY) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `A worked case through the combinator: a provider in a third country whose output is used in the Union, as a free and open-source AI system`

-- Limb (a) applies (the provider places a system on the market in the Union) and limb (c) applies; Article 2(12) excludes a free and open-source system that is none of the exceptions.
#ASSERT `Art 2 the Regulation applies given the answers of the paragraphs` (LIST (`Art 2(1)(a) the Regulation applies to the provider` (Date 2 2 2025) TRUE TRUE FALSE), (`Art 2(12) the Regulation applies to the AI system released under a free and open-source licence` (Date 2 2 2025) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The same provider, with the system now placed on the market as a high-risk AI system: the exclusion does not operate, and the limb decides.
#ASSERT `Art 2 the Regulation applies given the answers of the paragraphs` (LIST (`Art 2(1)(a) the Regulation applies to the provider` (Date 2 2 2025) TRUE TRUE FALSE), (`Art 2(12) the Regulation applies to the AI system released under a free and open-source licence` (Date 2 2 2025) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The same facts before Chapter I applies: every paragraph answers NOTHING, so the sum is NOTHING.
#ASSERT `Art 2 the Regulation applies given the answers of the paragraphs` (LIST (`Art 2(1)(a) the Regulation applies to the provider` (Date 1 2 2025) TRUE TRUE FALSE), (`Art 2(12) the Regulation applies to the AI system released under a free and open-source licence` (Date 1 2 2025) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS NOTHING
